ring-devices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"What paired devices can do"},"125":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#network-requirements","content":"Network requirements"},"126":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#troubleshooting-pairing","content":"Troubleshooting pairing"},"127":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#multiple-devices","content":"Multiple devices"},"128":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","content":"Gent lets you access your desktop sessions from any device on the same network. Your desktop is the server — it runs the terminals, AI agents, and editors. Paired devices are live mirrors that connect directly, with no cloud involved."},"129":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#how-pairing-works","content":"Gent uses multicast UDP for automatic device discovery on your local network. When two devices running Gent are on the same Wi-Fi or LAN, they find each other automatically. No manual IP entry, no account creation, no cloud relay."},"130":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#launch-gent-on-both-devices","content":"Open Gent on your desktop and on the device you want to pair (phone, tablet, or another computer)."},"131":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#wait-for-discovery","content":"Devices on the same network appear automatically in the sidebar within a few seconds. You will see the other device's name show up under the device list."},"132":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#tap-to-pair","content":"Select the discovered device in the sidebar. The first connection establishes the pairing. Once paired, the device remembers the connection for future sessions."},"133":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"Once paired, the remote device can:"},"134":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"View and interact with all terminal sessions running on the desktop"},"135":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"Chat with AI agents that are running on the desktop"},"136":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"Browse and edit files through the IDE"},"137":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"Preview web apps running on the desktop's localhost"},"138":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"Send and receive files"},"139":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#what-paired-devices-can-do","content":"Mobile devices (iOS/Android) do not run sessions locally. All terminals, agent chats, and IDE sessions live on the desktop. The mobile app is a remote viewer and controller."},"140":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#network-requirements","content":"Both devices must be on the **same local network** (same Wi-Fi or LAN)"},"141":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#network-requirements","content":"Gent uses TCP port **53317** by default for communication (configurable in Settings)"},"142":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-23","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#network-requirements","content":"Multicast UDP must not be blocked by your router — most home and office networks allow it"},"143":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-24","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#network-requirements","content":"No internet connection is required for pairing"},"144":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-25","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#troubleshooting-pairing","content":"If devices don't discover each other:"},"145":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-26","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#troubleshooting-pairing","content":"Confirm both devices are on the same Wi-Fi network"},"146":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-27","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#troubleshooting-pairing","content":"Check that no firewall is blocking port 53317 (TCP) or multicast (UDP)"},"147":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-28","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#troubleshooting-pairing","content":"On macOS, ensure Gent has local network permission in **System Settings > Privacy & Security > Local Network**"},"148":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-29","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#troubleshooting-pairing","content":"Try restarting Gent on both devices — this triggers a fresh multicast scan"},"149":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-30","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#troubleshooting-pairing","content":"If automatic discovery fails, check Remote Troubleshooting for manual connection options"},"150":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices-31","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/pairing-devices#multiple-devices","content":"You can pair multiple devices with the same desktop. Each paired device appears in the sidebar, and switching between them shows that device's remote sessions. Your local device is always listed first."},"151":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"page","content":"Agentic Mobile","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Integrations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent"},"152":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-0","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent","content":"An agentic toolkit to control, debug, and profile iOS and Android applications through the bundled Argent connector."},"153":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-1","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"What agents can do"},"154":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-2","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent#example-prompts","content":"Example prompts"},"155":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-3","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Platform requirements"},"156":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-4","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent#enabling-agentic-mobile","content":"Enabling Agentic Mobile"},"157":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-5","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent#permissions","content":"Permissions"},"158":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-6","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent#mobile-app-vs-agentic-mobile","content":"Mobile app vs Agentic Mobile"},"159":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-7","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/argent#related","content":"Related"},"160":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-8","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent","content":"Agentic Mobile in Gent is powered by Argent, the MCP toolkit from Software Mansion. It gives agents a real mobile-app control surface instead of limiting them to source-code edits."},"161":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-9","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent","content":"An agentic toolkit to control, debug, and profile iOS and Android applications. Your agent can navigate your app, explore the component tree, inspect network requests, and trace performance problems in your mobile apps."},"162":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-10","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent","content":"Gent bundles Argent as `@swmansion/argent`, so you can enable it from the connector library without manually installing the package."},"163":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-11","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Agentic Mobile is useful when the agent needs to work against the running app:"},"164":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-12","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Navigate iOS and Android screens"},"165":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-13","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Tap, swipe, pinch, rotate, and type"},"166":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-14","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Launch, restart, reinstall, or reload the app"},"167":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-15","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Take screenshots and compare screen states"},"168":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-16","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Explore the React Native component tree"},"169":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-17","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Inspect native view hierarchy"},"170":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-18","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Read network logs and request details"},"171":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-19","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Start and analyze React or native profiler sessions"},"172":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-20","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"Connect symptoms in the UI to source files, requests, and performance traces"},"173":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-21","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#what-agents-can-do","content":"The workflow is simple: the agent changes code, runs the app, drives the app, observes what happened, and keeps going."},"174":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-22","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Agentic Mobile runs from the desktop agent session. Your phone can control the Gent session remotely, but the simulator/emulator tooling runs on the paired desktop."},"175":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-23","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Platform"},"176":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-24","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Requirement"},"177":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-25","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"macOS"},"178":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-26","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Xcode for iOS simulators; Android SDK platform-tools and an emulator/AVD for Android"},"179":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-27","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Linux"},"180":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-28","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Android SDK platform-tools and an emulator/AVD"},"181":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-29","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Windows"},"182":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-30","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"Android SDK platform-tools and an emulator/AVD"},"183":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-31","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#platform-requirements","content":"iOS simulator control requires macOS and Xcode. Android requires `adb` plus a running emulator or configured AVD."},"184":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-32","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#enabling-agentic-mobile","content":"Open the Connectors UI"},"185":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-33","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#enabling-agentic-mobile","content":"Find **Argent**"},"186":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-34","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#enabling-agentic-mobile","content":"Enable it for the agent session"},"187":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-35","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#enabling-agentic-mobile","content":"Start or restart the agent chat so the CLI receives the MCP server config"},"188":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-36","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#enabling-agentic-mobile","content":"Argent does not require API credentials. It talks to local simulator/emulator tooling on your development machine."},"189":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-37","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#permissions","content":"Some Argent tools only read state, such as screenshots, hierarchy inspection, logs, and profiler queries. Other tools perform actions, such as tapping, swiping, launching apps, reloading Metro, or starting recordings."},"190":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-38","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#permissions","content":"Review action prompts the same way you would review shell commands: the agent is controlling a local simulator or emulator on your machine."},"191":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-39","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#mobile-app-vs-agentic-mobile","content":"Gent's iOS and Android apps let you control desktop sessions from your phone. Agentic Mobile is different: it lets the desktop agent control iOS and Android simulators/emulators for app development."},"192":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-40","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#mobile-app-vs-agentic-mobile","content":"Those two pieces work well together. You can start an agent task from your phone, let it drive a simulator on your desktop through Argent, and get the result back in the same Gent chat."},"193":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-41","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#related","content":"Agent Chat"},"194":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-42","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#related","content":"Mobile Usage"},"195":{"id":"/docs/integrations/argent-43","page_id":"/docs/integrations/argent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/argent#related","content":"Connector Setup"},"196":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"page","content":"Claude Code Integration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Integrations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code"},"197":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-0","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","content":"How Claude Code CLI works inside Gent's agent chat."},"198":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-1","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"199":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-2","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#requirements","content":"Requirements"},"200":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-3","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#features-in-gent","content":"Features in Gent"},"201":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-4","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#streaming-responses","content":"Streaming responses"},"202":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-5","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#tool-use-visualization","content":"Tool use visualization"},"203":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-6","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#conversation-persistence","content":"Conversation persistence"},"204":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-7","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#conversation-forking","content":"Conversation forking"},"205":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-8","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#mcp-connector-passthrough","content":"MCP connector passthrough"},"206":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-9","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#tool-approval","content":"Tool approval"},"207":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-10","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#remote-usage","content":"Remote usage"},"208":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-11","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#tips","content":"Tips"},"209":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-12","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","content":"Claude Code is the most deeply integrated AI CLI in Gent. Unlike Codex and Copilot (which run one-shot), Claude Code maintains a persistent process with multi-turn conversation support, making it feel like a native part of the app."},"210":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-13","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#how-it-works","content":"When you start an agent chat with Claude Code:"},"211":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-14","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#how-it-works","content":"Gent spawns the `claude` CLI with `--input-format stream-json` for streaming communication"},"212":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-15","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#how-it-works","content":"The process stays alive for the entire conversation — follow-up messages go through stdin"},"213":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-16","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#how-it-works","content":"Responses stream back in real time with text, tool calls, and results"},"214":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-17","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#how-it-works","content":"MCP connectors are passed via a generated config file"},"215":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-18","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#how-it-works","content":"This long-lived process model means there is no multi-second delay between messages. After the initial startup, follow-ups are instant."},"216":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-19","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#requirements","content":"You need the Claude Code CLI installed on your system:"},"217":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-20","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#requirements","content":"Gent detects available CLIs automatically. If `claude` is in your PATH, it appears as an option when creating an agent chat."},"218":{"id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code-21","page_id":"/docs/integrations/claude-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/integrations/claude-code#streaming-responses","content":"Text and tool use stream in real time. You see the agent's thinking as it happens, not